    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0196",
      "sequence": 208,
      "meaning": "No one knows this mystery; the sun continues on while singing the Lord’s virtues. Gods, sages and Nāgas behold the festival and return home recounting their good fortune. Śiva confides another secret to steadfast Girijā: he and Kākabhuśuṇḍi, unrecognized in human forms, roam the streets together, swelling with supreme bliss and lost in love. Only one upon whom Rāma bestows grace can know this auspicious event. At the celebration Daśaratha gives every visitor whatever pleases them—elephants, chariots, horses, gold, cows, diamonds and many garments—until all minds are satisfied. Everywhere people bless all four sons with long life, calling them Tulsīdāsa’s Lords.",
