    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0197",
      "sequence": 209,
      "meaning": "Some days pass without anyone noticing day or night. When the time for naming comes, the king summons the wise sage, worships him and asks him to choose names after reflection. Vasiṣṭha says the children have countless incomparable names, but he will name them according to his understanding: the ocean and treasury of bliss, one drop of whose joy satisfies the three worlds, is Rāma, abode of happiness and giver of rest to all. The one who bears and nourishes the universe is Bharata; the one whose remembrance destroys enemies is Śatrughna; the abode of auspicious marks, beloved of Rāma and support of the whole world, receives the noble name Lakṣmaṇa.",
