    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0199",
      "sequence": 211,
      "meaning": "Rāma’s dark infant body possesses the beauty of millions of Loves and the depth of blue lotus and raincloud. His red lotus feet and shining nails resemble pearls set upon petals; thunderbolt, banner and sprout marks shine there, and the anklets’ sound enchants sages. A tinkling girdle circles his waist; three lines mark the belly and his navel is profoundly deep. Broad ornamented arms, the lovely lion-claw charm at his heart, jewel necklaces and the Brahmin-foot mark adorn his chest. His conch-like throat, fine chin and face hold immeasurable beauty; paired baby teeth, red lips, nose and forehead mark defy description. Beautiful ears, lovely cheeks, sweet lisping speech, smooth curling hair and thick side-locks are arranged by his mother in many styles. Dressed in a yellow infant smock, he crawls on knees and hands—a sight dear to Śiva. Neither Vedas nor Śeṣa can describe this form; only one who has seen it even in a dream knows it. The holy couple’s supreme love makes the mass of joy, conqueror of delusion and one beyond knowledge and speech perform infant deeds.",
