    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0200",
      "sequence": 212,
      "meaning": "In this way Rāma, father and mother of the universe, gives happiness to Ayodhyā’s people. Śiva tells Bhavānī that this is the manifest destiny of those who love Raghunātha’s feet. What empty effort can free from worldly bonds one who turns away from Raghupati? The Lord’s māyā holds every moving and unmoving being under control and, frightened by a mere play of his brow, makes them dance. Why abandon such a Lord to worship another? Cast off cleverness in mind, deed and word and worship; Raghurāya will show grace. As the Lord performs infant sports, he delights the entire city: Kauśalyā sometimes holds and dandles him, sometimes lays him in a cradle and rocks him. Absorbed in love day and night, the mother loses all sense of time and, overcome by affection for her son, sings of his childhood deeds.",
